[SEVERITY: MEDIUM] — Global Exception Filters Swallow Critical Errors
What's wrong:
The GqlBadRequestHandler and GqlUnauthorizedHandler exception filters catch errors and re-throw them as GraphQL errors. However, they extract only the message and don't log the original error context, stack trace, or request ID. This makes production debugging nearly impossible.

Where exactly:

File: src/shared/exception/gql-bad-request.handler.ts
Line(s): 5-18
File: src/shared/exception/gql-unauthorized.handler.ts
Line(s): 5-15
Why it matters:
When errors occur in production, there's no way to correlate user-reported issues with server logs. The swallowed errors include validation failures, database constraint violations, and authentication issues—all critical for security monitoring.

Fix:
Add structured logging with correlation IDs:

typescript
@Catch(BadRequestException)
export class GqlBadRequestHandler implements GqlExceptionFilter {
    private readonly logger = new Logger(GqlBadRequestHandler.name);
    
    catch(exception: HttpException, host: ArgumentsHost) {
        const ctx = GqlExecutionContext.create(host);
        const requestId = ctx.getContext().req?.id || 'unknown';
        
        this.logger.error({
            message: 'Bad request exception',
            requestId,
            error: exception.message,
            stack: exception.stack,
            input: ctx.getArgs() // Be careful with PII
        });
        
        // ... existing transformation logic
    }
}
